 "wikidata": "Q2907541",
 "kit": "gabled_row",
 "about": "The rowing clubs' boathouses on the east bank of the Schuylkill below the Fairmount dam (1860-1904; a National Historic Landmark): stone or brick ground floors at the water, half-timber, stucco or shingle upper stories, and steep hipped, gabled and turreted dark roofs, outlined in lights at night. Each house is modeled on its own outline, with its club, date, style, materials, stories and roof form from the NHL nomination and its heights and roof color measured. #1 (Plaisted Hall) has no outline near the Row in the L&I or OSM data and is left out for now.",
